# ci/local.conf.example — template for YOUR machine's build configuration.
#
#   cp ci/local.conf.example ci/local.conf
#   $EDITOR ci/local.conf
#
# Then no per-run arguments are needed:
#
#   scripts/iris-build.sh --flavor o32 --version 1.0   # one flavor
#   scripts/release-local.sh                           # build both + publish
#
# The real ci/local.conf is .gitignore'd — personal paths and disk-image names
# never belong in the repo (see CLAUDE.md). This .example is the only
# committed copy.
#
# Format: KEY=VALUE, one per line, # comments. Values may be double-quoted
# (needed if a path contains spaces). The file is parsed, not sourced — no
# shell code runs from it. Precedence everywhere: command-line flag >
# environment variable of the same name > this file. The GitHub Actions
# workflow never reads this file (it is not committed); there the same
# variables arrive from repo secrets and dispatch inputs instead.

# ---- boot disks (the only settings most people need) ------------------------
# Installed IRIX system disks WITH the dev tools (cc, make, headers; Motif for
# the GUI). Root's password must be empty (or export IRIX_ROOT_PASSWORD).
#
# TIP: if your images live on a NAS/network share, point these at LOCAL copies
# — the emulator reads the disk constantly, and copy-on-write means the copy
# stays pristine anyway (writes go to <image>.chd.diff.chd next to it).

# IRIX 5.3 + IDO -> the o32 binaries (portable, run on IRIX 5.3-6.5)
IRIX53_IMAGE=/path/to/irix53-dev.chd

# IRIX 6.5 + MIPSpro -> the n32 binaries (faster, IRIX 6.x only)
IRIX65_IMAGE=/path/to/irix65-dev.chd

# No local file? A private download URL works instead of (or as a fallback
# for) each image — the same thing the IRIX53_DISK_URL/IRIX65_DISK_URL repo
# secrets do in CI. Accepts a bare .chd or a .zip containing one.
#IRIX53_DISK_URL=https://example.com/private/irix53-dev.chd
#IRIX65_DISK_URL=https://example.com/private/irix65-dev.zip

# ---- enable/disable a flavor -------------------------------------------------
# Only have one of the two images? Turn the other flavor off (0/no/false/off)
# and scripts/release-local.sh skips it; packaging adapts to what was built.
# (In CI the same switch is the build_o32/build_n32 dispatch input or the
# BUILD_O32/BUILD_N32 repo variable.)
#BUILD_O32=1
#BUILD_N32=1

# ---- Software Manager (inst/swmgr) distribution ------------------------------
# scripts/iris-gendist.sh builds a real inst-installable product natively with
# SGI's gendist in the 5.3 guest. gendist comes from the inst_dev.sw subsystem
# ("Software Packager") on the IRIS Development Option 5.3 CD — point this at
# that ISO and the script installs it into the guest's overlay automatically
# the first time (the boot image itself is never touched):
#IRIX53_IDO_ISO=/path/to/IRIS-Development-Option-5.3.iso
#
# If that inst session reports conflicts (e.g. a patch on your image that
# inst considers machine-incompatible under emulation), put the resolution
# choices here after reviewing them once — they are applied verbatim, never
# guessed (this is exactly what you'd type at the Inst> prompt):
#IDO_CONFLICT_CHOICES=1a
#
# Skip building the inst distribution entirely (it needs both flavors built):
#BUILD_INST=1

# ---- tools ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the iris emulator lives (default ../iris). Both a source build and a
# fetch-iris.sh download dir work — the scripts look for
# <dir>/target/release/{iris,iris-ci}. Relative paths are tried from your
# current directory first, then from the repo root.
#IRIS_DIR=../iris

# Which iris releases fetch-iris.sh pulls, and an optional version pin
# (default: danifunker/iris @ latest; don't pin before v2026-07-28-20-04 —
# older tags lack iris-ci outside linux x64/arm64).
#IRIS_RELEASE_REPO=danifunker/iris
#IRIS_TAG=v2026-07-28-20-04

# rb-cli binary to use (default: PATH, else ensure-rbcli.sh downloads one).
#RB_CLI=/usr/local/bin/rb-cli
